    "summary": "Adire cloth: composed of two even lengths of machine plain woven European cotton hand sewn together with raffia. The textile is decorated using the stitch-resist method. The producer has sewn the desired pattern into the textile before dyeing the textile indigo. The textile is divided into 24 regular oblongs  decorated with geometric shapes many of which are still sewn onto the textile.  This pattern is called ALABERE.  The textile is machine hemmed.",
